---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii1_5",
  "series": "Band II 1 (1663 - 1685)",
  "seq": 5,
  "text": "<p> [[10.1]] <b>5. CHRISTIAN DAUM AN LEIBNIZ</p>\n<p> [[10.2]] Zwickau, 30. März (9. April) 1666. [4.6.]</b></p>\n<p> [[10.14]] Leibnüzio. </p>\n<p> [[10.15]] Cl^#'m^#'e et PerEximie Vir. Fautor et Amice pl. colende. </p>\n<p> [[10.16]] Quam grata mihi Dissertatio tua acciderit, nolo verbis explicare. Sensi inde me beneficium\n[[10.17]] meum, si quod est, sic collocasse, ut beneficium contra mihi eo pepererim longe majus, ac\n[[10.18]] praestantius. Tu enim Clarissime Vir in theatrum Virorum eruditissimorum produxisti, quae ego\n[[10.19]] intra paucorum, talia etiam aegre capientium aut nil mirantium, modo non carpentium attegias,\n[[10.20]] ut sic dicam, conclusa habui hactenus. Unde debitorem me tibi agnoscis ingentem. De ipsa\n[[10.21]] Dissertatione tua quid dicam? Attonuisti novitate inventi, et singulari arte ingenii ruditatem\n[[10.22]] nostram. Quae, ubi otium dabitur pinguius, speculationes tamen illi suas qualesquales indulgebit\n[[10.23]] et de multis cogitabit penitius. Latum enim hic aperuisti campum ingeniosae ac subtili\n[[10.24]] industriae. Atque utinam in Mathesi aliquos fecissemus progressus, ut illis possemus sufficere:\n[[10.25]] Sane non frustra speraremus collocaturos nos operam huic negotio impendendam. Sed me\n[[11.1]] Genius meus olim ad omnia alia tulit, inviditque occasionem abnegans penitus: Nunc avocationes\n[[11.2]] et publica functio animum alio vertunt. Ita enim comparatae sunt res meae, ut ex quo\n[[11.3]] literas tuas aperuerim, vix dissertationem inspicere, nedum pellegere, et quod huic debetur,\n[[11.4]] religere licitum fuerit. Et praeterea statim ab oblatore tuarum ad responsum poscebar. Quod\n[[11.5]] ecce jam habes subitum satis ac insubidum, sed non solum. </p>\n<p> [[11.6]] Mitto enim una inspiciendum, quem non vidisse ais Publilium Optat. Porphyrium Velserianae\n[[11.7]] et Pythoeanae Editionis, quod nonnihil varient, libros inter meos rarissimos charissimosque.\n[[11.8]] Addidi et ipsum Reimerum nuper frustra quaesitum, cum Reineccelio, ne quid alieni\n[[11.9]] in armum tollam, qui sub finem fere Opusculi sui <i>Proteo</i> suo ansam dedit mihi ulterius\n[[11.10]] progrediendi. Eum olim scriptum cum literis antequam excuderetur, mecum communem faciebat\n[[11.11]] D. Theod. Steinmetzius Lipsiensis p[iae] r[ecordationis], pueritiae meae Fautor et instimulator\n[[11.12]] unicus; in cujus gratiam multa alia talia tum musinabar, sed quae periere paullo post\n[[11.13]] dum infelici illo tempore sortis pila hinc inde jactitarer. </p>\n<p> [[11.14]] Goldsteinii <Fn><i>Am Rande, von Daums Hand, zwei Kolonnen Zahlen zur Berechnung seines 55. Geburtstages.</i></Fn> Opusculum non habeo. Kleppisium multos ante annos visum, ante paucos\n[[11.15]] demum nactus sum. Proteus meus ultimus ulterius variari potest si caesuram negligere velis, ut\n[[11.16]] vides in MS^#'t^#'o quod una recipis, sed cum caeteris remittendum. Illos enim delevi cum chartam\n[[11.17]] non suffecturam clamarent operae. <i>Vertumni</i> mei (cujus 4. Millenarius in scriniis ineditus adhuc\n[[11.18]] latet) Proteos illos nescio an bene sic indigitarim; nec feceram ad Te, nisi memoria officio suo\n[[11.19]] defuisset. Compendifaciendi enim laboris et reiterationis gratia ita appellaram inibi. </p>\n<p> [[12.1]] Cum heri meum Natalem 55. celebrassem, visa tua hodie dissertatione, subiit in illum\n[[12.2]] novus hic Proteus: <i>Haec Lux, ne crux sit, fac Dux bone, qui regis axem!</i> Vel ita: <i>Haec lux, ne\n[[12.3]] crux trux sit, fac dux, qui regis axem.</i> Tu supputa, si tanti, quot vicibus variari queat. Hactenus,\n[[12.4]] subsecivis semihorulis, ne otiarer, diversos versus ex Anthologia diverso habitu indui, forte si\n[[12.5]] videbitur doctis, publico daturus, et hactenus excusos illos simul, qui pene in spongiam, ut\n[[12.6]] Augusti Ajax ceciderant, nisi tu, Vir Eruditissime retentasses. Haec dum scribo, dum libros\n[[12.7]] quos mitterem conquiro, incidit et alius Bauhusii Proteus lib. 2. <i>Epigr.</i> 69. cujus nescio an\n[[12.8]] mentionem feceris, nondum enim ut dixi, perlegi integrum tuum Opusculum: <i>Rex, Dux, Sol,\n[[12.9]] Lex, Lux, Fons, Spes, Pax, Mens, Petra, Christus.</i> Sed non possum non adjicere varias esse\n[[12.10]] quoque posse facies Palindromorum, ut nuper in <i>fabulis</i> Hieron. Osii observavi hoc distichon: </p>\n<p> [[12.11]] <i>Cur durante die tantum Canis alligor inquit:</i> </p>\n<p> [[12.12]] <i>Acris ut esse queam nocte cadente vigil.</i>\n [[12.13]] Habes hic duos Anacreonticos: </p>\n<p> [[12.14]] <i>Vigil cadente nocte Queam esse ut acris inquit</i> </p>\n<p> [[12.15]] Et Trochaicum: </p>\n<p> [[12.16]] <i>Inquit alligor canis tantum die durante cur.</i> </p>\n<p> [[12.17]] Sed satis nugatus sum et turbor quoque a nescio quo interpellatus. Tu, Clarissime Vir quod\n[[12.18]] coepisti perge favere mihi, et nos plura talia doce. B.V. et Salve. Cygn. d. 30 Martii 1666. </p>\n<p> [[12.19]] Clariss. T. Praestantiae </p>\n<p> [[12.20]] Omni studio atque officio. </p>\n<p> [[13.1]] Clariss. et PerEximio Viro Dⁿ^#'o Gotfredo Guilielmo Leibnüzio Phil. Mag. et J.U. Baccal.\n[[13.2]] etc. Fautori et Amico suo pl. colendo. </p>\n",
  "number": "5.",
  "title": "CHRISTIAN DAUM AN LEIBNIZ",
  "date": "Zwickau, 30. März (9. April) 1666. [4.6.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:5. CHRISTIAN DAUM AN LEIBNIZ Zwickau, 30. März (9. April) 1666. [4.6.] Leibnüzio. Cl^#'m^#'e et PerEximie Vir. Fautor et Amice pl. colende. Quam grata mihi Dissertatio tua acciderit, nolo verbis explicare. Sensi inde me beneficium meum, si quod est, sic collocasse, ut beneficium contra mihi eo peper...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>